G = {}
G['plant-upgradations'] = [
 ('Start with a bottleneck study, not a shopping list','Many upgrade projects begin with a new machine that turns out not to be the constraint. A short study of the line, comparing rated and actual output at each step, shows where product actually waits. Often the limit is a utility such as steam, compressed air or cooling water, and a modest change there releases more capacity than an expensive new process machine would.'),
 ('Rank upgrades by payback and risk','Once the constraints are known, each option is costed and its saving estimated. Energy upgrades such as variable speed drives, condensate recovery, insulation and heat recovery usually pay back fastest. Automation and safety upgrades are judged on quality, labour and risk reduction as well as cost. A ranked list lets management approve the work in stages that match its budget.'),
 ('Plan the work around production','Upgrades are most disruptive when they stop a running factory. Seamens plans tie-ins, shutdowns and testing around your production calendar, preparing as much as possible in advance so the actual stop is short. Where a plant runs continuously, temporary connections and phased changeovers keep output going while the new equipment is installed.'),
 ('Measure the result after commissioning','Every upgrade should be proven. Energy meters, production counts and quality records taken before the project are repeated afterwards so the saving or capacity gain is shown in figures. This evidence helps justify the next stage of investment and gives your management team confidence in the results.'),
 ('Keep drawings and documents current','An upgraded plant needs updated drawings, control logic and maintenance schedules. Handover includes the changed documents so your maintenance team knows exactly what was installed and how to look after it, avoiding confusion years later when the original project team has moved on.'),
 ('Safety comes with every change','Any change to pressure systems, electrical panels or guarding is reviewed for safety before work starts. Upgrades are an opportunity to bring older equipment closer to current practice, for example adding interlocks, relief devices or emergency stops where they were missing.')]
G['mechanical-maintenance-contracts'] = [
 ('What a contract covers','A maintenance contract defines a list of assets, such as pumps, fans, gearboxes, compressors, boilers and cooling towers, and sets a schedule of inspections and servicing for each. The scope, response times and reporting are written down, so both your team and Seamens know exactly what is included and how performance will be judged.'),
 ('Condition monitoring finds faults early','Vibration analysis and thermography detect bearing wear, misalignment, imbalance, loose connections and overheating long before a breakdown. Readings are trended at each visit, and a rising trend triggers planned repair at a convenient time instead of an emergency stop in the middle of a production run.'),
 ('Planned work costs less than breakdowns','A breakdown brings lost output, overtime, rushed parts and sometimes secondary damage to other components. Planned replacement of a bearing or seal is far cheaper. Over a year, a contract usually moves most maintenance work from the emergency column to the planned column.'),
 ('Reports your management can use','After each visit you receive a short report showing what was checked, what was found and what is recommended. Over time this becomes an asset history that supports budgeting, spare parts planning and decisions about when to replace rather than repair equipment.'),
 ('Working alongside your own team','Contracts are designed to support, not replace, in-house maintenance staff. Seamens engineers bring specialised tools and experience, while your team handles daily checks. Many clients use the visits as on-the-job training for their technicians.'),
 ('Emergency response when it is needed','Even well-maintained plants have unexpected failures. Contract clients receive priority breakdown response, with engineers who already know the equipment and its history, which shortens diagnosis and repair time.')]
G['erection-commissioning'] = [
 ('One accountable partner','On many projects, equipment suppliers, civil contractors, pipefitters and electricians each work to their own scope, and problems fall between them. A turnkey arrangement gives one party responsibility for coordinating the work and delivering a working system, which simplifies management for the plant owner.'),
 ('Pipework and instrumentation done properly','Correct pipe sizing, supports, slopes, valves and instruments decide how well a cooling tower, chiller or RO plant will perform. Seamens installs pipework and instruments to the design, pressure tests the system and checks that every instrument reads correctly before start-up.'),
 ('Commissioning is a structured process','Commissioning follows a sequence: mechanical completion checks, flushing and cleaning, energising and rotation checks, functional tests of controls and alarms, and finally performance testing at load. Each step is recorded, and issues are closed out before the next step begins.'),
 ('Performance testing proves the design','A system is only complete when it delivers its design duty. Performance tests measure flow, temperature, pressure and water quality against the specification. The results are written into the handover report so you have evidence that the plant meets what was ordered.'),
 ('Training and handover','Operators and maintenance staff are trained on the new equipment, including normal operation, alarms and routine maintenance. Handover documents include as-built drawings, test records, manuals and recommended spares.'),
 ('Support after start-up','The first months of operation often reveal small adjustments. Seamens remains available after handover to fine-tune controls, review performance and support your team as the plant settles into routine operation.')]
G['custom-fabrication'] = [
 ('Built to your layout','Standard catalogue equipment does not always fit an existing building, a tight boiler room or an unusual process. Custom fabrication produces tanks, vessels, ducts and supports sized for your space and duty, which can save the cost and delay of modifying the building around off-the-shelf equipment.'),
 ('Choosing the right material','Mild steel is economical for many structures, ducts and water tanks, while stainless steel suits chemical, food and corrosive duties. The choice depends on the liquid or gas handled, temperature and cleaning needs. Seamens reviews the duty with you and recommends the material and thickness before fabrication starts.'),
 ('Quality in welding and testing','Good fabrication depends on qualified welders, correct joint preparation and inspection. Welds are inspected and tanks are leak or pressure tested where required, so the finished item is fit for service when it arrives on site.'),
 ('Ventilation and exhaust systems','Hot, humid or dusty production halls need effective exhaust. Seamens fabricates ductwork and supplies industrial belt-drive exhaust fans, sized for the air volume and resistance of the system, to improve working conditions and protect equipment.'),
 ('Installation included','Fabricated items are delivered and installed by the same team, including lifting, alignment, connections and supports. This removes the gap between a fabricator and an installer and reduces the risk of items not fitting on site.'),
 ('Repairs and modifications','Fabrication is not only for new items. Worn tanks, damaged ducts and corroded supports can often be repaired or modified, extending their life at a fraction of replacement cost.')]
G['industrial-spare-parts'] = [
 ('Correct identification first','Most delays with spare parts come from ordering the wrong item. Sharing the equipment make, model, serial number, part number and a photo, or the old part itself, lets Seamens identify the correct replacement and avoid a second order.'),
 ('Critical spares on the shelf','For equipment whose failure stops production, keeping critical spares in stock is cheaper than waiting. Seamens can help you list critical items, such as pump seals, bearings and key valves, so the most important parts are always available.'),
 ('Pump parts that restore performance','Worn impellers, failed mechanical seals and noisy bearings reduce pump flow and efficiency. Replacing them with correct parts restores the pump to its design duty and reduces energy use.'),
 ('Heat exchanger tubes and plates','Leaking tubes or damaged plates mix fluids and reduce heat transfer. Correct replacement tubes, plates and gaskets bring the exchanger back to duty and prevent contamination.'),
 ('Valves and actuators','Valves that pass or stick cause control problems and waste. Replacement valves and actuators restore reliable isolation and control.'),
 ('Learning from failures','When a part fails early, the cause matters as much as the replacement. Seamens can review the failure, such as misalignment, poor lubrication or wrong material, so the new part lasts longer.')]
G['plant-erection-installation'] = [
 ('Foundations decide long-term reliability','Machines that vibrate on weak or poorly levelled foundations wear bearings and couplings quickly. Seamens checks foundation drawings, levels and anchor positions before equipment arrives, so installation proceeds smoothly and machines run smoothly for years.'),
 ('Careful lifting and placement','Heavy equipment must be lifted with the right cranes, slings and procedures. Planned lifting protects both people and equipment, and placement is checked against layout drawings before grouting.'),
 ('Alignment and levelling','Shaft alignment between motors, pumps, fans and gearboxes is critical. Laser or dial alignment to tolerance reduces vibration, power loss and early failure.'),
 ('Pipework built and tested','Pipework is fabricated, erected and supported to drawings, then pressure tested before insulation and start-up, so leaks are found when they are easy to fix.'),
 ('Pre-commissioning checks','Before energising, every item is checked: lubrication, rotation, guards, instruments, electrical terminations and safety devices. A documented checklist means nothing is missed.'),
 ('Coordinated with your production','On running sites, erection is coordinated with production so that tie-ins and shutdowns are short and planned.')]
G['textile-machinery-parts'] = [
 ('Parts matched to your machine','Loom and frame parts must match the make and model exactly. Sharing the machine details and part numbers lets Seamens supply the right part first time for rapier, projectile and air-jet looms, spinning frames and finishing machines.'),
 ('Wear parts that affect fabric quality','Worn healds, reeds and picker sticks cause fabric faults such as broken ends, reed marks and weak picks. Replacing wear parts on schedule protects fabric quality as well as machine uptime.'),
 ('Stenter and dryer parts','Chains, clips, pins and bearings on stenters affect width control and fabric marks. Good parts keep finishing ranges running at speed.'),
 ('Reducing downtime','Imported parts can take weeks. A local source for common parts shortens stops and reduces the stock a mill must hold.'),
 ('Planning spares by machine count','Mills with many identical machines can plan spares by consumption. Seamens can help build a usage-based spares list.'),
 ('Quality checked on arrival','Parts are checked for dimensions and finish so they fit and perform as expected.')]
G['monitoring-controls'] = [
 ('Why automatic dosing beats manual dosing','Manual dosing depends on each operator on each shift. Doses are missed, doubled or guessed. Automatic dosing pumps, linked to flow or a controller, add chemical steadily so water treatment stays within its target range around the clock.'),
 ('Online TDS and pH','Online sensors measure boiler and cooling water continuously. A controller opens blow-down when TDS rises and adjusts dosing when pH drifts, saving water, chemical and fuel compared with fixed timers.'),
 ('Alarms that protect equipment','Alarm limits warn operators when water quality moves out of range, so action is taken before scale or corrosion begins.'),
 ('SCADA connectivity','Controllers can connect to plant SCADA, so engineers see water treatment data alongside production data and keep historic records.'),
 ('Maintenance of sensors','Sensors need cleaning and calibration. Seamens sets a simple calibration routine so readings stay accurate.'),
 ('Fits existing plants','Dosing pumps and controllers can be retrofitted to existing boilers and towers without major work.')]
G['reverse-osmosis-ro-plants'] = [
 ('Design starts with water analysis','An RO plant is designed around a full raw water analysis: TDS, hardness, silica, iron, organics and bacteria. These figures decide pre-treatment, membrane type, recovery and chemical programme. Skipping this step is the most common cause of plants that foul quickly.'),
 ('Pre-treatment protects membranes','Ultra-filtration, media filters, softening or cartridge filters remove what would foul the membranes. Good pre-treatment is the difference between membranes lasting years and months.'),
 ('Choosing single or double pass','Single-pass RO suits most process and drinking water. Double-pass is used where very low TDS is needed, such as high-pressure boiler feed.'),
 ('Concentrate and ZLD','Concentrate disposal is planned at design stage. Where discharge is restricted, Zero Liquid Discharge systems recover water and reduce waste.'),
 ('Operating the plant well','Logging normalised flow, pressure and conductivity shows when cleaning is needed.'),
 ('Chemical programme included','Anti-scalant, biocide and membrane cleaners keep the plant performing.')]
G['industrial-chiller-systems'] = [
 ('Sizing on actual load','Chillers sized from a nameplate guess often run oversized and inefficient. Measured or calculated cooling load, with allowance for growth, gives the right capacity and better part-load efficiency.'),
 ('Air-cooled or water-cooled','Water-cooled chillers are more efficient but need a cooling tower and water treatment. Air-cooled units are simpler where water is scarce. The choice is made for your site.'),
 ('Screw and centrifugal options','Screw chillers cover 50 to 2,000 TR; centrifugal chillers suit large loads. Selection balances efficiency, cost and load profile.'),
 ('Cold storage design','Cold stores need insulation, door design and refrigeration matched to product and throughput.'),
 ('Water treatment protects efficiency','Scale in condensers raises power use. A treatment programme keeps chillers efficient.'),
 ('Maintenance and support','Regular servicing keeps chillers reliable.')]
G['captive-power-plant-support'] = [
 ('Water chemistry is availability','In a captive power plant, boiler tube failures and turbine deposits cause forced outages. Strict feed water and steam purity control is one of the most effective ways to keep the plant available and avoid costly grid purchases.'),
 ('Feed water treatment','Oxygen scavenging, pH control and hardness control protect boiler tubes. Programmes are set to the boiler pressure and design.'),
 ('Cooling water programmes','Condensers and engine coolers need scale, corrosion and biological control.'),
 ('Turbine deposit control','Carryover of silica and salts deposits on turbine blades, reducing output. Monitoring steam purity limits this.'),
 ('Regular review','Monthly data review keeps programmes on target.')]
G['industrial-air-humidification'] = [
 ('Humidity and yarn performance','Cotton yarn loses strength and builds static in dry air. Controlled humidity in spinning and weaving halls reduces breaks and fly.'),
 ('Choosing the system','High-pressure fogging, ultrasonic humidifiers and evaporative pads each suit different spaces. Selection follows a site assessment.'),
 ('Control and sensors','Sensors and control panels hold humidity at target automatically.'),
 ('Water quality','Treated water prevents nozzle blocking and hygiene problems.'),
 ('Cooling benefit','Evaporative systems also cool halls in summer.')]
